            "review_text": "Alvin Low\n14 contributions\n0\nMy 1st Omakase Yakiniku Experience\nJul 2019 • Couples\nBooking - 3/5\nI dined at the restaurant on a Saturday 13th July 2019 and was well greeted and seated on a nice table on the second level. I was allocated the 9 pm slot (no earlier reservations) although when I arrive at the restaurant it was less than full. I figured it was a new restaurant and staffing was the main reason for the late allocation. \n\nAtmosphere - 4/5\nThey have a lovely bar. I would recommend coming in for a drink earlier to appreciate the design and soak in the atmosphere. \n\nService - 2.5/5\nThe manager and some of the staff were able to speak in English & Japanese (thumbs up). However the allocation of staff per table was disorganized. With multiple staff serving each table (junior and senior) they were unsure of the cut of meat, dishes were served before completing each dish (omakse). But personally the biggest sin is the staff were not trained well in cooking the meat.\n\nFood - 3.5/5\nThe quality of cuts was excellent. I must say this is my first Yakiniku Omakase and I am not sure if the size of the meat cuts or the utensils need refining? But I feel the courses needs a little more attention, curation and diversity. \n\nQuality - 4/5\nThe salad was excellent and so was the premium steak cut. Again the staff should at least ask or explain what level should the meat be cooked too. Otherwise it is a waste of good produce. \n\nOverall - 3/5\nI would recommend this restaurant for couples and first dates. Great atmosphere and I believe the food and service will improve in the near future.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten July 25, 2019",
